IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`

-- je54-art08-bankruptcy: Article 8 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, "Meaning of bankruptcy".
-- In every enactment, a reference to a person becoming bankrupt is, unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to one of the listed events, and a reference to bankruptcy is to be construed accordingly.
-- The list grew by amendment: limb (ba) is in all seven texts; the bank limb arrived 31 January 2022 as (f) and became (g) on 1 September 2022; the limited liability company limb arrived 1 September 2022 as (f); the
-- administration order limb (ea) arrived 19 June 2026.  Which text governs a question about an event is fork I2 (NOTES.md section 6): the text in force on the day of the event (taken, as the brief directs) or the text
-- in force on the day on which the question about the event is asked.  Each of the two is callable; the first function in this module takes the text as an input and says nothing about which day chose it.
-- The list is read as the complete list ("construed as references to either"): an event that is on none of the limbs of the text read is not a person becoming bankrupt for the purposes of any enactment under this Article.
-- The Law does not say whether a limited liability company or a bank is also a "company"; the person's kind is the caller's input.

§ `Article 8: Meaning of bankruptcy`

-- src:29 | In every enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, references to a person becoming bankrupt shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as references to either –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8 (src:29)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 8: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 8 does not say what a reference to a person becoming bankrupt then means"

-- src:30 | (a) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to place the person’s property under the control of the Court (de remettre ses biens entre les mains de la Justice);
-- src:31 | (b) the declaring of the property of that person to be en désastre;
-- src:32 | (ba) the grant by the Viscount of a debt remission order in respect of that person’s qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016;
-- src:33 | (c) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to make a general cession of the person’s property (de faire cession générale de tous ses biens-meubles et héritages);
-- src:34 | (d) a decision of the Royal Court adjudging the property of that person to be renounced (adjugée renoncée);
-- src:35 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:36 | (ea) in the case of a company, the making of an administration order under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:37 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:38 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8 (src:30-38)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 8: no paragraph of the text lists the event` MEANS
    REFUSE "no paragraph of this text of Article 8 lists the event"

-- The bank limb: (f) in V2b (31 January 2022), (g) from V2c (1 September 2022).
-- src:l_17_1954_20220831:36 | (f) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
-- src:l_17_1954_20240110:37 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
-- src:l_17_1954_20251123:37 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
-- src:l_17_1954_20260618:37 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
-- src:38 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8, limb for a bank (src:l_17_1954_20220831:36), (src:l_17_1954_20240110:37), (src:l_17_1954_20251123:37), (src:l_17_1954_20260618:37), (src:38)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8: the text has the limb for a bank` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `V2b, 31 January 2022 to 31 August 2022` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2c, 1 September 2022 to 10 January 2024` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2d, 11 January 2024 to 23 November 2025` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2e, 24 November 2025 to 18 June 2026` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The limited liability company limb: (f) from V2c (1 September 2022).
-- src:l_17_1954_20240110:36 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:l_17_1954_20251123:36 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:l_17_1954_20260618:36 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:37 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8, limb for a limited liability company (src:l_17_1954_20240110:36), (src:l_17_1954_20251123:36), (src:l_17_1954_20260618:36), (src:37)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8: the text has the limb for a limited liability company` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `V2c, 1 September 2022 to 10 January 2024` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2d, 11 January 2024 to 23 November 2025` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2e, 24 November 2025 to 18 June 2026` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The administration order limb (ea): V2f only (19 June 2026).
-- src:36 | (ea) in the case of a company, the making of an administration order under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8, limb (ea) for an administration order (src:36)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8: the text has the limb for an administration order` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether a text of Article 8 lists an event.  The six limbs (a), (b), (ba), (c), (d) and (e) are in every deposited text.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:33 | (a) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to place the person’s property under the control of the Court (de remettre ses biens entre les mains de la Justice);
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:34 | (b) the declaring of the property of that person to be en désastre;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:35 | (ba) the grant by the Viscount of a debt remission order in respect of that person’s qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:36 | (c) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to make a general cession of the person’s property (de faire cession générale de tous ses biens-meubles et héritages);
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:37 | (d) a decision of the Royal Court adjudging the property of that person to be renounced (adjugée renoncée); or
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:38 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991,
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:30 | (a) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to place the person’s property under the control of the Court (de remettre ses biens entre les mains de la Justice);
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:31 | (b) the declaring of the property of that person to be en désastre;
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:32 | (ba) the grant by the Viscount of a debt remission order in respect of that person’s qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016;
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:33 | (c) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to make a general cession of the person’s property (de faire cession générale de tous ses biens-meubles et héritages);
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:34 | (d) a decision of the Royal Court adjudging the property of that person to be renounced (adjugée renoncée); or
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:35 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991,
-- src:30 | (a) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to place the person’s property under the control of the Court (de remettre ses biens entre les mains de la Justice);
-- src:31 | (b) the declaring of the property of that person to be en désastre;
-- src:32 | (ba) the grant by the Viscount of a debt remission order in respect of that person’s qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016;
-- src:33 | (c) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to make a general cession of the person’s property (de faire cession générale de tous ses biens-meubles et héritages);
-- src:34 | (d) a decision of the Royal Court adjudging the property of that person to be renounced (adjugée renoncée);
-- src:35 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8, limbs (a) to (e) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:33-38), (src:l_17_1954_20220130:30-35), (src:30-35)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      e IS AN `Event in the life of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8: the text lists the event` v e MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER e
               WHEN `the Royal Court grants the person's own application to place the person's property under the control of the Court` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the person's property is declared en désastre` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the Viscount grants a debt remission order in respect of the person's qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the Royal Court grants the person's own application to make a general cession of the person's property` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the Royal Court adjudges the person's property to be renounced` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `a company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `an administration order is made in respect of a company under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN `Article 8: the text has the limb for an administration order` v
               WHEN `a limited liability company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022` THEN `Article 8: the text has the limb for a limited liability company` v
               WHEN `a bank winding up order is made under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017` THEN `Article 8: the text has the limb for a bank` v
               WHEN `some other event` THEN FALSE

-- The limbs that begin "in the case of a company", "in the case of a limited liability company" and "in the case of a bank" apply only to a person of that kind; the other limbs say "that person".
-- src:35 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:36 | (ea) in the case of a company, the making of an administration order under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:37 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:38 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8, limbs (e), (ea), (f) and (g) (src:35-38)
GIVEN e IS AN `Event in the life of a person`
      person IS A `Person who may have become bankrupt`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8: the person is of the kind that the limb names` e person MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN person's `is a company`
    WHEN `an administration order is made in respect of a company under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN person's `is a company`
    WHEN `a limited liability company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022` THEN person's `is a limited liability company`
    WHEN `a bank winding up order is made under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017` THEN person's `is a bank`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The question Article 8 answers: is this event a person becoming bankrupt, on the text read?
-- src:29 | In every enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, references to a person becoming bankrupt shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as references to either –
-- src:30 | (a) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to place the person’s property under the control of the Court (de remettre ses biens entre les mains de la Justice);
-- src:31 | (b) the declaring of the property of that person to be en désastre;
-- src:32 | (ba) the grant by the Viscount of a debt remission order in respect of that person’s qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016;
-- src:33 | (c) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to make a general cession of the person’s property (de faire cession générale de tous ses biens-meubles et héritages);
-- src:34 | (d) a decision of the Royal Court adjudging the property of that person to be renounced (adjugée renoncée);
-- src:35 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:36 | (ea) in the case of a company, the making of an administration order under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:37 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:38 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
-- src:39 | and references to bankruptcy shall be construed accordingly.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8 (src:29-39)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      e IS AN `Event in the life of a person`
      person IS A `Person who may have become bankrupt`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8: the event is a person becoming bankrupt` v e person `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 8: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE `Article 8: the text lists the event` v e AND `Article 8: the person is of the kind that the limb names` e person

-- The paragraph of the text that lists the event.  The bank limb moves from (f) to (g) when the limited liability company limb is inserted before it.
-- src:30 | (a) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to place the person’s property under the control of the Court (de remettre ses biens entre les mains de la Justice);
-- src:31 | (b) the declaring of the property of that person to be en désastre;
-- src:32 | (ba) the grant by the Viscount of a debt remission order in respect of that person’s qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016;
-- src:33 | (c) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to make a general cession of the person’s property (de faire cession générale de tous ses biens-meubles et héritages);
-- src:34 | (d) a decision of the Royal Court adjudging the property of that person to be renounced (adjugée renoncée);
-- src:35 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:36 | (ea) in the case of a company, the making of an administration order under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:37 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:38 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8 (src:30-38)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      e IS AN `Event in the life of a person`
GIVETH A STRING
`Article 8: the paragraph of the text that lists the event` v e MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Article 8: the text lists the event` v e THEN `Article 8: no paragraph of the text lists the event`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER e
               WHEN `the Royal Court grants the person's own application to place the person's property under the control of the Court` THEN "(a)"
               WHEN `the person's property is declared en désastre` THEN "(b)"
               WHEN `the Viscount grants a debt remission order in respect of the person's qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016` THEN "(ba)"
               WHEN `the Royal Court grants the person's own application to make a general cession of the person's property` THEN "(c)"
               WHEN `the Royal Court adjudges the person's property to be renounced` THEN "(d)"
               WHEN `a company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN "(e)"
               WHEN `an administration order is made in respect of a company under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` THEN "(ea)"
               WHEN `a limited liability company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022` THEN "(f)"
               WHEN `a bank winding up order is made under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017` THEN
                   CONSIDER v
                   WHEN `V2b, 31 January 2022 to 31 August 2022` THEN "(f)"
                   OTHERWISE "(g)"
               WHEN `some other event` THEN `Article 8: no paragraph of the text lists the event`

-- Fork I2: which day selects the text of Article 8.
-- src:29 | In every enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, references to a person becoming bankrupt shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as references to either –
-- src:30 | (a) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to place the person’s property under the control of the Court (de remettre ses biens entre les mains de la Justice);
-- src:31 | (b) the declaring of the property of that person to be en désastre;
-- src:32 | (ba) the grant by the Viscount of a debt remission order in respect of that person’s qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016;
-- src:33 | (c) the grant by the Royal Court of an application made by that person to make a general cession of the person’s property (de faire cession générale de tous ses biens-meubles et héritages);
-- src:34 | (d) a decision of the Royal Court adjudging the property of that person to be renounced (adjugée renoncée);
-- src:35 | (e) in the case of a company, the winding up of the company by means of a creditors’ winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:36 | (ea) in the case of a company, the making of an administration order under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:37 | (f) in the case of a limited liability company, the winding up of a limited liability company by means of a creditors’ winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022; or
-- src:38 | (g) in the case of a bank, the making of a bank winding up order under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017,
-- src:39 | and references to bankruptcy shall be construed accordingly.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8 (src:29-39)
GIVEN selecting IS A `Which day selects the text for Article 8`
      `the day on which the event happened` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that selects the text of Article 8` selecting `the day on which the event happened` `the day on which the question is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER selecting
    WHEN `the day of the event` THEN `the day on which the event happened`
    WHEN `the day on which the question about the event is asked` THEN `the day on which the question is asked`

-- Fork I2, taken: the text in force on the day of the event (the brief directs this; assumed, not ruled).  The other reading is `the day on which the question about the event is asked`.
